{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/externalclientallowedresources"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"D3"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the audiences an externally registered client may address. The single most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"important field on this policy, and the reason the settings handler refuses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dynamic_registration: anonymous"},{"type":"text","text":" while it is empty. A client an unrelated party"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered cannot declare its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"allowed_resources"},{"type":"text","text":"; it inherits this list verbatim,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so what a stranger can mint a token "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"for","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a decision the tenant took in advance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than one the registration request makes. Empty means an externally registered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client can obtain only today’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam:user"},{"type":"text","text":" tokens — which AXIAM’s own APIs accept. That"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is why the interlock exists: the empty list is not a safe default for an "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"open"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registration endpoint, it is the most dangerous one. Shared with T5 (CIMD), which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inherits the same list for the same reason."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":